  "slide_mu": "kinetic friction while the contact point slips (skidding, check, spin-back)",
  "roll": "rolling deceleration a = roll_decel + roll_c1 * v (m/s^2); greens take it from stimp: 1.83^2 / (2 * stimp_ft * 0.3048)",
  "static_factor": "a ball at rest stays at rest while the slope's pull g sin(theta) / (1 + k) is at most static_factor * roll_decel; at least 1, or a ball stops and restarts on a slope forever",
  "plug_speed": "a normal impact speed above this plugs the ball (soft surfaces only)"
